  "audit_id": "cluster-bootstrap-data-availability-audit-v1",
  "conclusion": {
    "data_ask": {
      "gap": "Per-test-row (or, minimally, per-test-polymer-aggregated) actual log10(melt viscosity) values AND both FFW_B3 and ML_B4 model predictions for the 194 polymer-safe test rows / 13 test polymers, persisted as a new signed JSON array (e.g. a polyverse_melt_viscosity_ffw_vs_ml_per_row_predictions receipt) alongside the existing aggregate FFW-vs-ML KPI.",
      "missing_arrays": [
        "test_row_polymer_id (length 194, one of 13 unique values)",
        "test_row_y_true_log10_viscosity (length 194)",
        "test_row_y_pred_B3_ffw_linear_mw_and_arrhenius_t (length 194)",
        "test_row_y_pred_B4_full_histgbm (length 194)"
      ],
      "source_of_truth": "These would be produced by the same harness that generated polyverse_melt_viscosity_fox_flory_whitten_physical_baseline_receipt.v1.json and the ML B4 HistGBM fit referenced by the FFW KPI -- re-run that harness with per-row prediction logging enabled and sign the resulting array as a new receipt. No new external data acquisition is required; this is a re-run-and-persist gap in the existing pipeline, not a missing dataset."
    },
    "genuine_cluster_bootstrap_executable_from_signed_artifacts": false,
    "n_candidate_per_row_or_per_polymer_prediction_arrays_found": 0,
    "quarantine_confirmation": "amphora-viscosity-score/reference/mvp20/quarantine/feedback_v2/exclusions/polyverse_melt_viscosity-3cd923b4d67399f9.json confirms partition=QUARANTINE_EXCLUDED, status=EXCLUDED_BY_RIGHTS, random_row_split_forbidden=true for the underlying row-level dataset; this audit did not open the row-level CSV or its .jsonl.gz shadow.",
    "reasoning": "A cluster bootstrap of R2(FFW_B3) - R2(ML_B4) requires, for each of the 13 test polymers, that polymer's per-row actual log10(viscosity) values and BOTH models' per-row predictions, so that resampled polymer sets can be re-scored. Every signed artifact examined (FFW KPI, FFW scientific receipt, conformal+AD KPI, conformal+AD scientific receipt, parent model receipt, and the prior disclosure-gap audit receipt) persists only AGGREGATE statistics over the full 194-row test set or its 5 applicability-domain quintiles (r2, rmse, mae, pearson_r, quintile coverage) -- never a per-row or per-polymer residual, prediction, or (actual, predicted) pair for either the FFW_B3 or ML_B4 model. Aggregate R2/RMSE cannot be decomposed back into per-polymer contributions without the underlying rows, so the pre-registered protocol cannot be executed without either (a) new signed per-row prediction arrays being added to the pipeline's model/KPI receipts, or (b) opening the quarantined Polyverse row-level CSV, which is out of scope for this item and this cron's rights authority."
  },
